 |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nNow, we work out the $y$ values using $y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$ This gives\n\n| **$\\theta $** | $0$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ | $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ | $\\pi $ | $\\frac{4\\pi }{3}$ | $\\frac{5\\pi }{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $7$ | $\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $-7$ | $-\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{7}{2}$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $0$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $-\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nPlotting these points, we obtain the following curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973156/assets/debf9475589e7e242df986d1fffb8a97834d6ce550279fc82b0428001b661eaa.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275672 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9e34dba-6df9-5555-903f-97eb3da427b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e34dba-6df9-5555-903f-97eb3da427b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275674} :answer-field/id #uuid "935309e2-1d8b-5d0b-9910-0c3b89a84ea0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9748b3ab-2088-5dba-a49d-2e58b8f44d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9748b3ab-2088-5dba-a49d-2e58b8f44d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275676} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a3520c1-4593-5c9f-bceb-5e6e6b1fe671" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e8fc38-c87a-543b-9fcb-b804965ed003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23e8fc38-c87a-543b-9fcb-b804965ed003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275678} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f92bc1e-818c-5856-a65b-3d8fc1ed0aac" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275677} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a3bc4e1-6e8d-5c3c-b9b9-7a5a3317106f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275680}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a3bc4e1-6e8d-5c3c-b9b9-7a5a3317106f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275680} :answer-field/id #uuid "5dc32d3c-367a-5cb0-8eb5-ec45bbd858c5" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275679}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7d27dc41-abce-5a21-8f11-4131f79addb5" :question/math-academy-id "q-326304" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=4t-{t}^{2},\\,y={t}^{2}+3,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ we can start by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t-{t}^{2} \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t) \\\\  & =-({t}^{2}-4t+4)+4 \\\\  & =-(t-2)^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-(t-2)^{2}+4\\le 4,$ we conclude that the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\le 4.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ notice that ${t}^{2}+3\\ge 3.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275681 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3cbf0ad0-a7c5-5c0f-a06c-9210fdc244ef" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d273ae97-5497-581e-8fc9-861e87494d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275683} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e984b-ee7a-529e-8f64-af65b7b25327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\le" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d273ae97-5497-581e-8fc9-861e87494d29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275683} :answer-field/id #uuid "8be93969-bc66-5853-bce2-2466b4b1e026" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275682} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4647b180-43dd-5ef7-9e55-30f96a53049f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275686}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4647b180-43dd-5ef7-9e55-30f96a53049f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275686} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd855a9-f7df-5452-aa72-f0275ed4eab6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275685} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "679e25d9-f485-543c-9368-d4b45a7f85d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "679e25d9-f485-543c-9368-d4b45a7f85d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ge" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275688} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ea9e0de-85bb-5c1e-a757-67dea78748eb" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275687} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e200f3-282c-54f2-bbbb-b408e9b7aa6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30e200f3-282c-54f2-bbbb-b408e9b7aa6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275690} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab796f89-d49c-5fb9-83cf-e9d4dddef621" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275689}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4e1822d2-5ae3-55a7-b554-0b016472863b" :question/math-academy-id "q-327851" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{4t}+1,\\,y=\\sqrt{t}+2,\\,t\\ge 0,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}$,\\,y$\n{{field-3}}{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each variable in turn.\n\n- To find the range of $x,$ note that $\\sqrt{4t}+1\\ge 1$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, the range of $x$ is\n\n$$\nx\\ge 1.\n$$\n\n- To find the range of $y,$ note that $\\sqrt{t}+2\\ge 2$ for all $t\\ge 0.$ Consequently, the range of $y$ is\n\n$$\ny\\ge 2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cddc940d-2185-569c-a62b-b507e95d3c35" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Range of a Parametric Equation Defined in Terms of Trigonometric Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1439d71d-e477-5ab7-a9df-19d21bf0a7ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1439d71d-e477-5ab7-a9df-19d21bf0a7ae" :answer/type {: